  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Life and Peace Institute</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life and Peace Institute, 2017-2022, The Ethiopia Program - Life and Peace Institute, 2017-2021, The Ethiopia Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Life and Peace Institut har ans&#xf6;kt som st&#xf6;d hos ambassaden f&#xf6;r sin verksamhet i Etiopien 2017-2020. Life and Peace ans&#xf6;ker om ca 31 MSEK. Denna insats omfattar ett samarbete med och finansiellt st&#xf6;d till organisationen Life and Peace Institute och dess verksamhet i Etiopien. Insatsen syftar till att bryta negativa sociala m&#xf6;nster och andra strukturella hinder f&#xf6;r fred och bidra till dialog och samarbete &#xf6;ver religi&#xf6;sa och etniska gr&#xe4;nser. LPI ska samarbeta med n&#xe5;gra nyckelakt&#xf6;rer som &#xe4;r universitet (l&#xe4;rare och studenter), interreligi&#xf6;sa r&#xe5;det, Ministry of Federal affaris och Peace and Develoment Center. De bed&#xf6;ms alla vara strategiska samarbetspartners f&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; m&#xe5;len. LPI planerar bidra till att skapa plattformar f&#xf6;r dialog och samarbete, bedriva forskning och kapacitetsutveckling av sina partners s&#xe5; de mer kompetent och professionellt kan axla en fredsbyggande roll.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Life and Peace Institute (LPI) has applied to Sida for funding of approximately 31 MSEK to carry out its Ethiopia Program during the period 2017-2020. The total budget of the intervention is 45,3 MSEK. The program is currently partially funded by two donors, namely, USAID and Swedish Mission Council(SMC). USAID funds one project of the program with a contribution of 11,1 MSEK for the whole program period while SMC is a program-wide donor with a contribution of 3,2 MSEK for 2017-2018.

The intervention aims at contributing to reducing negative relational social patterns and support a culture of trust and collaboration between otherwise segregated or conflicted social groups by facilitating dialogue, research and collaborative action on local level and engaging relevant decision-makers and policy implementers to enhance structural conditions for peace.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the proposed intervention is to contribute to reducing negative relational social patterns and support a culture of trust and collaboration between otherwise segregated or conflicted social groups (could be based on ethnicity, religion, residential areas... etc, people that normally do not meet and engage in dialogue) by facilitating dialogue, research and collaborative action on local level and engaging relevant decision-makers and policy implementers to enhance structural conditions for peace.</narrative>
  </description>
